1.0-0
   o	forked children (fork=TRUE) no longer try to re-seed the
	system RNG (the code was never active). They inherit the R RNG
	state of the parent, see ?webstart for how to get independent
	random streams.

   o	forked children now exit with _exit() and stdio is flushed
	before fork(). Previously a child could emit output buffered
	by the parent again or, when run by Rscript, make the parent
	continue reading its script from the wrong position.

   o	use withVisible() instead of the non-API R_Visible in
	R >= 4.6.0.

   o	support chunked request bodies (Transfer-Encoding: chunked).
	The chunks are collected into the request body, so handlers
	see the same as with Content-Length. Other transfer codings
	are still answered with 501, Transfer-Encoding together with
	Content-Length, in HTTP/1.0 or with GET/HEAD with 400.

   o	reject header fields with whitespace between the name and the
	colon with 400 (RFC 9112, 5.1). Previously such Content-Length
	or Transfer-Encoding fields were ignored, so the body was parsed
	as the next request (request smuggling).

   o	1xx, 204 and 304 responses no longer include a body or
	Content-Length, which broke the framing of keep-alive
	connections.

   o	reject requests with more than one Host: header with 400
	(RFC 9112, 3.2).
